- Check what OS you are running on, use the appropriate commands (e.g. Windows use PowerShell).
- You don't seem to have a good grasp on QB64, make sure you review the documentation for QB64 when making changes.
- QB64 is located in c:\code\hutsell\qb64pe, the binary is qb64pe.exe
- Whenever doing a hard-coded date use local system functions to check the date/time rather than your own imagination.
## testing
- we change tests to match the codebase, not vice versa.

## documentation
- Continue to add documentation for new functions as code evolves
- Review documentation for accuracy when code changes
### Standard Documentation Template
```qb64
'============================================================================
' FunctionName - Brief description
'============================================================================
' Parameters:
'   param1 (TYPE) - Description
'   param2 (TYPE) - Description
' Returns:
'   TYPE - Description
' Description:
'   Detailed description of what the function does.
'   Include any important notes about behavior, side effects, etc.
' Side Effects:
'   - List any side effects (if applicable)
'============================================================================
```